// Rule: [T1213.002] UNC6671 - Scripted Sharepoint File Access
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1213.002
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Sentinel / Log Analytics
// Required telemetry: OfficeActivity
// Purpose: Hunt for SharePoint or OneDrive file access performed through scripting clients observed in cloud data-theft operations.
// Logic: Evaluate OfficeActivity for scripted sharepoint file access using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A scripting client accessed a SharePoint or OneDrive file under an identified account and requires ownership and session validation.
// A match does not prove: File download, bulk collection, sensitive content, successful exfiltration, malicious intent or UNC6671 attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// UNC6671 - scripted SharePoint or OneDrive file access
// Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Sentinel / Log Analytics
// Telemetry: Microsoft 365 connector -> OfficeActivity
//
// GTIG recommends treating FileAccessed as seriously as FileDownloaded when
// UserAgent identifies a scripting library. FileAccessed records access, not
// confirmed download or exfiltration. Validate every match against approved
// automation, service ownership, user/session context and accessed resources.

OfficeActivity
| where Operation == "FileAccessed"
| where UserAgent startswith "python-requests/"
    or UserAgent startswith "WindowsPowerShell/"
    or UserAgent startswith "Go-http-client/"
| project TimeGenerated,
          UserId,
          UserType,
          ClientIP,
          UserAgent,
          OfficeWorkload,
          Site_Url,
          SourceRelativeUrl,
          SourceFileName,
          OfficeObjectId,
          IsManagedDevice,
          ResultStatus,
          OfficeId
| order by TimeGenerated desc
